'''Terrelian Jango Jumpers''' were tall, slender [[humanoid]]s who were known for their acrobatic abilities.<ref name="DB">{{Databank|terrelian-jango-jumper|Terrelian Jango Jumper}}</ref> The criminal [[Cassilyda Cryar|Cassilyda "Cassie" Cryar]] was a Terrelian Jango Jumper,<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" /> as were the [[Eighth Brother]], a member of the [[Galactic Empire]]'s [[Inquisitorius]],<ref name="Eighth Brother">{{Databank|eighth-brother-inquisitor|Eighth Brother Inquisitor}}</ref> and [[Lika]], who was held captive by [[Trandoshan]] [[big game hunter]]s.<ref name="EpGuide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/padawan-lost-episode-guide|text="Padawan Lost" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

==Biology and appearance==
Terrelian Jango Jumpers were a tall [[humanoid]] [[species]] with [[Color|multi-colored]] skin<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" /> that could vary from gray<ref name="Twilight" /> to blue or white. They possessed acrobatic abilities that enabled them to perform high jumps. The [[thief]] [[Cassilyda Cryar|Cassie Cryar]] used this to her advantage to leap onto rooftops on [[Coruscant]] when chased by the [[Jedi]] [[Padawan]] [[Ahsoka Tano]].<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" />

==Behind the scenes==
Terrelian Jango Jumpers first appeared the episode "[[Lightsaber Lost]]" of ''[[The Clone Wars: Season Two]]''.<ref name="Lightsaber Lost" /> The design of the character [[Lika]], who appeared in the later episode "[[Padawan Lost]]," was based on the character model of Cryar.<ref name="EpGuide" />

